  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e89ac9b32d19465c8a6cd64ced4e709b, type: 3}
  m_Name: Prompt_16
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Actors.AI.LlmAI.LlmPromptSo
  prompt: "# \U0001F6A2 TURN-BASED NAVAL STRATEGY \n\n## 1. YOUR OBJECTIVE\n**Win
    condition:** Destroy all enemy ships (\U0001F6A2).  \nYou are @faction@. You
    control the @faction@ ships.\nYour enemies are from these [@enemy_factions@]
    factions.\n\n---\n\n## GAME MECHANICS & STRATEGIC PRIORITY\nYour core directives
    are:\n1. **TARGET PRIORITIZATION**: Consistently selecting and hitting enemies
    is the #1 driver of success.\n2. **LEVERAGE WAVES FOR ADVANTAGE**: Waves can
    be used to move you by 1 extra tile (50% chance) and to extend your attacks by
    1 tile (100% chance). Be careful to not walk on top of waves by mistake, because
    that might stop your movement.\n3. **MOVE AND ATTACK**: After you move, you **can
    and should** attack if a valid enemy target comes into range. When choosing where
    to move, first check if moving there will put any enemies within your attack
    range (@attack_range@ tiles) and outside your offset (@attack_offset@ tiles).
    If it will, that is often the best move. Failing to attack an enemy that is in
    your range leaves you vulnerable to their counter-attack during their turn.\n---\n\n##
    TACTICAL RULES & DECISION FLOW\n\n**A. ATTACK PHASE (Your First Priority)**\n-
    **Can you attack a VALID target RIGHT NOW?**\n    - **VALID TARGETS:** `Enemy
    Ship (\U0001F6A2)` or `Neutral Target (\U0001F3AF)`. Attacking `Ally Ship` or
    `Empty Tile` is a game-losing mistake.\n    - **RANGE/ OFFSET:** Target must
    be away from you by @attack_offset@ units tiles (Manhattan distance), but no
    more than @attack_range@.\n    - **ATTACK RING:** Your attack area must be calculated
    using your position (`@self_x@`, `@self_y@`) and these positions: `(+0,+2)`,
    `(+0,-2)`, `(+2,+0)`, `(-2,+0)`, `(+1,+1)`, `(+1,-1)`, `(-1,+1)`, `(-1,-1)`.\n-
    **Wave-Extension Tactic:** If no enemy is in direct range, check if attacking
    a `Wave` tile (`~^`, `~V`, etc.) would extend your shot to hit an enemy/target.
    Waves follow these rules:\n    - `~^` (North) \u2192 `(x, y+1)`\n    - `~v` (South)
    \u2192 `(x, y-1)`\n    - `~>` (East) \u2192 `(x+1, y)`\n    - `~<` (West) \u2192
    `(x-1, y)`\n\n**B. MOVEMENT PHASE**\n- **Purpose:** Move to achieve one of these
    goals:\n    1. **Close Distance:** To get a priority enemy into your attack range.\n   
    2. **Line Up Shot:** To position yourself to use a wave for an extended attack
    next turn or attack an enemy.\n    3. **Evade Danger:** To move away from clusters
    of enemies or dangerous wave paths.\n    4. **Get Together:** To move closer
    to your allies. Attacking as a group increases your chances of eliminating one
    enemy faster before a counterattack.\n- **Recalculate after choosing:** After
    deciding your movements, recalculate the Manhattan distances to check if the
    new position matches your reasoning.\n---\n\n## CURRENT STATE & ANALYSIS\n\n-
    **Your Ship:** `@self_status@` at (`@self_x@`, `@self_y@`)\n- **Enemies:** \n@grid_overview_enemies@\n-
    **Wave Analysis:** \n@grid_overview_waves@\n- **Movement Options:**\n@safe_movement_positions@\n-
    **Current Targets (if you do not move):**\n`@current_attack_positions@`\n---\n\n##
    RESPONSE FORMAT\n- Output the positions (x,y) for where you want to move (movement),
    attack, and where to move after attacking (move_after_attack). Moving after an
    attack will happen even if the attack fails or is invalid. If, for any of these,
    you decide to not do, then return [-1, -1], for any of these fields. Do not return
    `null` for any field - instead, return [-1, -1].\n**CRITICAL:** Output **ONLY**
    a valid JSON object. No other text.\n```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"Concise tactic,
    e.g., 'Wave-extended attack on low-health enemy'\",\n  \"movement\": [x1, y1],\n 
    \"attack\": [x2, y2],\n  \"move_after_attack\": [x3, y3]\n}"
  includeEmptySpaces: 0
